#====================================================================
# E329 - Prune a bundled database client graph for OHOS CMake cross builds
#====================================================================

id:                     E459
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake
phase:                  configuration|build|package
error_signature:        FindCurses|MYSQL_CHECK_RPC|cannot execute.*target|Permission denied.*symlink|try_run

severity:               3
category:               cmake, cross-compile, conan, client-library, openharmony
match_keywords:         WITHOUT_SERVER, OHOS, HMDFS, TARGET_FILE, FindCurses, MYSQL_CHECK_RPC, bundled, try_run, client library, target usage requirements, SunRPC
title:                  Prune a bundled database client graph for OHOS CMake cross builds

root_cause:             A large CMake database source tree keeps server-oriented checks, bundled helper targets, convenience symlinks, and target executables in a client-only cross-build graph. OHOS CMake and HMDFS expose these assumptions as configure, build, or packaging failures.
affected_scope:         Conan 2 recipes that build a client/library subset from a MySQL-compatible or similarly structured CMake monorepo for an OHOS AArch64 target.
verification_cmd:       apply the portability patch to a clean source tree; configure with the OHOS profile and client-only options; inspect custom commands and output directories; build and package the static client; compile and run a C consumer on the target

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           semantic-client-graph-pruning
rec_description:        Keep the target OS module selected by upstream CMake, disable server-only features, skip unused RPC/configure probes, resolve build tools with TARGET_FILE, avoid HMDFS convenience symlinks, provide explicit dependency cache variables, make each helper target own its compile dependencies, and mirror platform include conditions in unit-test targets.
rec_command:            cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Linux -DOHOS=ON -DWITHOUT_SERVER=ON -DWITH_ROUTER=OFF -DWITH_NDB=OFF
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe|cmake-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      reduce-package-surface
fallback_description:   Build the static client package first and defer server, router, shared helper, and full upstream server-test validation until their OHOS dependency and runtime contracts are available.
fallback_command:       set WITHOUT_SERVER=ON and validate a real downstream C consumer before widening the package surface
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          package-options|test-package

forbid_1_pattern:       execute.*target.*binary|bare.*PATH.*generator|unversioned.*system.*tool
forbid_1_reason:        A cross-built target executable is not runnable on the build host, and a PATH lookup can select an incompatible generator.
forbid_1_consequence:   Generated sources become non-reproducible or the build fails after configuration.

forbid_2_pattern:       ln -s.*OHOS|symlink.*HMDFS|keep.*convenience.*symlink
forbid_2_reason:        HMDFS-backed build paths may reject convenience symlinks even when the real output directory is valid.
forbid_2_consequence:   Configure or install fails after the useful target artifacts have already been built.

forbid_3_pattern:       patch.*generated.*tirpc|enable.*RPC.*client-only|claim.*full.*server.*test
forbid_3_reason:        The client-only package does not consume the server RPC graph, and the current evidence does not cover the full mysqld runtime.
forbid_3_consequence:   The recipe gains fragile generated-source changes or overstates its validation boundary.

